dataset(wages).glm(union ~ educ, family: binomial, link: probit).summary(exponentiate: true)
error[Z0401]: `exponentiate:` needs a logit link: the coefficients of a probit link are not logarithms of a ratio
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:88
  |
1 | dataset(wages).glm(union ~ educ, family: binomial, link: probit).summary(exponentiate: true)
  |                                                                                        ^^^^ the link is probit
  |
  = help: odds ratios belong to `link: logit`; `margins` gives the effects of any binary fit as changes in the probability

====
dataset(wages).reg(log(wage) ~ educ).summary(exponentiate: true)
error[Z0401]: `exponentiate:` is for a `glm` fit with a logit link: the coefficients of `reg` are differences in the outcome, not logarithms of a ratio
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:60
  |
1 | dataset(wages).reg(log(wage) ~ educ).summary(exponentiate: true)
  |                                                            ^^^^ not for a regression
  |
  = help: where the outcome is in logs, one coefficient is exponentiated by hand: `exp(fit.coef(x))`

====
