dataset(sleep).t_test(extra, group: group).summary(exponentiate: true)
error[Z0401]: `exponentiate:` is for a fitted model: a test's result has no coefficients
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:66
  |
1 | dataset(sleep).t_test(extra, group: group).summary(exponentiate: true)
  |                                                                  ^^^^ not for a test
  |
  = help: a `glm` fit with a logit link gives odds ratios: `fit.summary(exponentiate: true)`

====
dataset(wages).glm(union ~ educ, family: binomial).summary(standardized: true, exponentiate: true)
error[Z0401]: `standardized:` is for a regression: a `glm` fit has no standardized coefficients in this release
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:74
  |
1 | dataset(wages).glm(union ~ educ, family: binomial).summary(standardized: true, exponentiate: true)
  |                                                                          ^^^^ not for a fit by maximum likelihood
  |
  = help: to compare regressors on one scale, standardize them before fitting: `add(z = standardize(x))`

